<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad ibn Said ibn Harun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad ibn <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-ibn-harun">Said ibn Harun</a> was the second and last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Santa Maria del <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a>, the small Muslim principality centred on the town later called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faro">Faro</a>. He succeeded his father Said ibn Harun and tried to balance between the Taifa of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silves">Silves</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>. Around 1051 he surrendered his town to al-Mutadid of the Taifa of Seville.</p></div>
